    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20824" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hĭulco</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, ātum,
			1, v. a.
			hiulcus, <i>to cause to gape</i> or <i>split open</i>, <i>to break into
				chinks</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum gravis exustos aestus hiulcat agros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					68, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per hiulcatos agros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fortun. Carm. 6, 12, 6</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
